IO-31: accept the deprecated [REPORT] NODESTATS keyword instead of reading it as NODES

report_readOptions() finds the keyword with findmatch(), which accepts any
token that starts with a keyword. ReportWords lists NODE before NODESTATS, so
"NODESTATS YES" was read as a node list and failed with ERROR 209 "undefined
object YES"; the branch that ignores NODESTATS could never run. Select that
branch when the token is NODESTATS.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-31_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/report.c b/src/legacy/engine/report.c
index 604507d..63218e4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/report.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/report.c
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ int report_readOptions(char* tok[], int ntoks)
     if ( ntoks < 2 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_ITEMS, "");
     k = (char)findmatch(tok[0], ReportWords);
     if ( k < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[0]);
+    if ( match(tok[0], w_NODESTATS) ) k = 9;  // NODE is a prefix of NODESTATS
 
     // --- keyword not SUBCATCHMENT, NODE, or LINK
     if (k < 2 || k > 4)
